{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Attempt-3 remediation (all 6 findings verified against source and fixed): (F1/F2) next_batch.py:536 and field_reads.py:88 both emit the literal 'ticket_not_found' — removed the invented next_batch_failed/field_read_failed from KNOWN_ERROR_CODES and the census. (F3) The claim/transition concurrency failure is ConcurrencyMismatch(CommandError) at txn.py:50 which carries NO error_code; classifier now isinstance-maps BOTH ConcurrencyMismatch AND library ConcurrencyError to concurrency_conflict, checked before the error_code branch. (F4/F6) RebarError/ConcurrencyError/TrackerRootError set returncode/stderr but NO .message; guard now uses str(exc) not exc.message (would AttributeError on the concurrency path). (F5) TicketNotFoundError raised ONLY at reads.py:310/313 (identical message); reads.py:469 'does not exist' stays bare ReadError and reads_cli.py:410 stays message-keyed, so deps_failed vs ticket_not_found is byte-identical (AC6). Verified LLMError exists (llm/errors.py:11, a RuntimeError, caught explicitly)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786151796402370001,"uuid":"67cedfd5-e401-461d-b38d-b02d42fbde16"}